I avoid narrow ice bridges; you can drown in case you're the target of
a fire breath or fire ray. (I drowned once on Medusa; got hit by a
wand of fire from a water troll.) Though not realistic in Real Life, I
suppose a wide path of ice in Nethack would provide a "safe place" to
be rescued (haven't checked, though).

Getting swarmed by monsters is a rare case on the rare water levels.
On water levels a wide path has the additional advantage that you can
stay away from the sea creatures and their specific attacks.

With the extreme radius of the cone of cold it is really a fascinating
attack. I should try it in a real game (as opposed to Witmode) on next
occasion.

